            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mjk"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Rating the recipe as is. It is wonderful. It is a little sweet for me but I have my own recipe which is a bit more involved: \nCut squash in half, lengthwise. Bake skin-side up, cut-side down, until it is done. Turn over and use fork to pull up strands. Mix butter, brown sugar, a small can of mandarin oranges and a 1/2 cup of sliced almonds. Toss. Put it back into the shell and place it back in the oven for 10 minutes to heat through. Family loves this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-12T16:05:42.507Z"
          },
          {
